# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Pjotrs Žguns et al. (2025). Benchmarking CHGNet Universal Machine Learning Interatomic Potential against DFT and EXAFS: The Case of Layered WS2 and MoS2.
#   Journal of Chemical Theory and Computation. doi:10.1021/acs.jctc.5c00955  arXiv:2509.08498v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2509.08498v1 (sha256 dc4e6bf7e59bba7f...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 228 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zguns2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the pretrained CHGNet v0.3.0 (registry model) and CHGNet
# fine-tuned on PBE-D3 relaxation snapshots of 2Hc-WS2 with 7,000, 350, 70
# and single frames; their energy, force and stress MAEs on the test sets
# TS1-TS4 as stated in the text (Sec. 3.1). MoS2 results and the
# learning curve are shown only in figures; EXAFS comparisons are not
# accuracy metrics of the schema.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
