###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Fine-tuning on 7,000 frames takes about 4,000 s on two 20-core Intel Xeon
# Gold 6148 processors, proportionally less for smaller sets (Sec. 2.2).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Energy MAEs are computed after shifting CHGNet energies by a constant (86 meV/atom for the pretrained, 1.5 meV/atom for the fine-tuned model) to align with DFT on an absolute scale (Fig. 2 caption).
# - The pretrained model's energy MAE is only in the Fig. 2 legend; its stress MAE against PBE without D3 (about 0.3 GPa) is not encoded.
# - MoS2 fine-tuning results (Figs. S5, S6), elastic constants and phonons are in the SI and not encoded. Which CHGNet layers stay frozen is in Table S3.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zguns2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

